<!--
=====================================================================
S92 · THE LAST BATON — A Golden-Hour Relay Finish
14 s · 1280x720 · 24 fps · MeshAsset cage modeling for the hero props
=====================================================================

COMPOSITION
  Two Character1 runners storm the home straight under a low sun. The
  hero holds a MeshAsset baton, breaks the tape at the MeshAsset finish
  arch, decelerates and raises the baton while his rival closes in.

  MESHASSET SHOWCASE (the point of this example)
    baton core   · 6 swept rings, tapered, pinned tips, 48 verts
    baton grip   · fatter swell ring pinned caps, 24 verts
    runner caps  · crown fan + bands + pinned flat brim, 30 verts
    arch posts   · 6-level curved/tapered column, 48 verts
    arch crown   · arced tube swept along x, drooping pinned ends, 40 verts
  Every prop above is authored from a catmull-clark control cage; no GLB,
  no external mesh file. The GLB is used for the runners only.

  STORY BEATS
    0.0 - 4.3  side-tracking shot · the chase, dust of the crowd behind
    4.3 - 8.5  arch cam · tape break, deceleration, rival crosses late
    8.5 - 14.0 push-in · the baton raise, two celebration cap tosses,
             confetti, title card

  ACTING
    One humanoid skeleton, four imported landing-page Actions sequenced
    by time: run -> walk stop -> victory wave (hero) and run -> walk
    stop -> catch-breath idle (rival). Locomotion is in-place; world
    travel is driven by deterministic position keyframes so foot IK and
    grounding stay exact.

  Light: low warm sun key with the only shadow map, cool sky fill, ACES
  at golden-hour white balance, exponential warm haze, a restrained
  bloom that flares through the finish, deterministic grain.
=====================================================================
-->
